# hai_world_parity (2026-11-23): the JavaScript port (docs/world.js) and the C op (ops/hai_world.c) run the SAME commands and must give the SAME words, the same exit codes, byte-identical ledgers
# and BYTE-IDENTICAL FRAMES (the canvas RGBA). The expected text was recorded once from the C op (whose rules case hai_world checks) and is literal: a mutant in EITHER implementation turns a row red.
# Steps cover every wall edge, the inner wall block, diagonals, a taken cell, teleport and bad input. Needs node and cmp. DEBT: absolute repo paths.
